n" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493} :db/id 17592186495003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "If $\\frac{z}{3}-2y=1$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate the variable $z.$ To do this, we treat $y$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nFirst, we add $2y$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{z}{3}-2y & =1 \\\\ \\frac{z}{3}-2y+2y & =1+2y \\\\ \\frac{z}{3} & =1+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{z}{3} & =1+2y \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{z}{3} & =3\\cdot (1+2y) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot \\frac{z}{\\cancel{3}} & =3\\cdot (1+2y) \\\\ z & =3\\cdot (1+2y) \\\\ z & =3\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2y \\\\ z & =3+6y\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186064349 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186063938 :question/id #uuid "3237ac51-d473-548d-b316-9425717c22bb" :question/math-academy-id "e-12907"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74cfd55f-4e24-5f97-ba42-28fa410866a7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048213} {:db/id 17592186049846}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186064589 :question/id #uuid "e8d042d4-df69-520c-9937-a83c21b7496c" :question/math-academy-id "q-21557"} {:db/id 17592186064609 :question/id #uuid "8d25c94b-41b9-50c7-83f2-16519ac89670" :question/math-academy-id "q-22227"} {:db/id 17592186064610 :question/id #uuid "123e3583-ff33-59f9-933c-26e880160316" :question/math-academy-id "q-22230"} {:db/id 17592186488243 :question/id #uuid "a062c0fa-ba5c-540d-bad1-e5dc2b1fdc72" :question/math-academy-id "q-176623"} {:db/id 17592186488244 :question/id #uuid "a390d02a-3ecf-5fc0-8eb1-0f04dc4eff6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-178606"} {:db/id 17592186495060 :question/id #uuid "131ccfe9-849e-53c3-a3f1-91aed4a65240" :question/math-academy-id "q-22237"} {:db/id 17592186495079 :question/id #uuid "42436934-3a89-50ee-8455-624cf79683ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-17658