lem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a+b?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2b=6a+14 \\\\ 5b+25=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2b=6a+14 & \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 5b+25=0. & \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2),$ we can solve for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5b+25 & =0 \\\\ 5b & =-25 \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-5$ into equation $(1)$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-5) & =6a+14 \\\\ -10 & =6a+14 \\\\ -10-14 & =6a \\\\ 6a & =-24 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=-5.$ So,\n\n$$\na+b=-4+(-5)=-4-5=-9.\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186048216} {:db/id 17592186048646} {:db/id 17592186048873} {:db/id 17592186048975} {:db/id 17592186048991} {:db/id 17592186049144} {:db/id 17592186049198} {:db/id 17592186049869} {:db/id 17592186050326} {:db/id 17592186050365} {:db/id 17592186050564} {:db/id 17592186050661} {:db/id 17592186050754} {:db/id 17592186050788} {:db/id 17592186050926} {:db/id 17592186050964} {:db/id 17592186050974} {:db/id 17592186050984} {:db/id 17592186051014} {:db/id 17592186078529 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186078153 :question/id #uuid "0690af9e-ae28-50a0-b2fd-0a9c3baaec3e" :question/math-academy-id "e-1280"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c12f648d-f276-5123-b6aa-b222ad108825" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049089} {:db/id 17592186050495}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186079068 :question/id #uuid "0257ed16-40ad-5cd9-b690-7fdf0fd13b32" :question/math-academy-id "q-52124"} {:db/id 17592186079149 :question/id #uuid "c069927d-2180-5264-8073-e7d8030f6d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-61823"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Polynomial Terms"} {:db/id 17592186078153 :question/id #uuid